\ kernel-native.4 - the native kernel's back end (docs/NATIVE.md, N1c-2;
\ Iteration 623 begins it): the words of kernel.4's part 9 that lay CV8's
\ code, for x86-64 - what the native kernel's own compiler uses when it
\ compiles at run time. forth/native-cross.4 skips kernel.4's definitions
\ of these names and compiles this file after part 9; a common word's
\ call to one before it is a forward call, resolved here.
\
\ The target has no assembler: these lay the machine code's bytes with
\ C, - the same instruction sequences native.4's templates lay at cross
\ time. The data stack: its top in rbx, the rest under rbp. A created
\ word's body is 24 bytes - push the data's address, a ret at 15, nops -
\ the data at the next 64-byte boundary, a line of its own - data written
\ beside code is self-modifying code to the processor (NATIVE.md 9); DOES>
\ puts a jump where the ret is, and >BODY reads the address in the mov. An inline
\ primitive's body begins EB 01 len: COMPILE, copies its len bytes.
CROSS-COMPILE

\ ---- laying bytes --------------------------------------------------------------
: ,4 ( n --- )   DUP C, 8 RSHIFT DUP C, 8 RSHIFT DUP C, 8 RSHIFT C, ;
: !4 ( n a-addr --- )
  >R  DUP R@ C!  8 RSHIFT DUP R@ 1+ C!  8 RSHIFT DUP R@ 2 + C!  8 RSHIFT R> 3 + C! ;
: @4 ( a-addr --- n )   \ unsigned
  DUP C@  OVER 1+ C@ 8 LSHIFT OR  OVER 2 + C@ 16 LSHIFT OR  SWAP 3 + C@ 24 LSHIFT OR ;
: PUSH, ( --- )   72 C, 131 C, 237 C, 8 C,  72 C, 137 C, 93 C, 0 C, ;  \ sub rbp,8  mov [rbp],rbx
: POPF, ( --- )   \ the top into rax, the stack popped, rax tested
  72 C, 137 C, 216 C,  72 C, 139 C, 93 C, 0 C,  72 C, 131 C, 197 C, 8 C,  72 C, 133 C, 192 C, ;
\ (693) Every relative field a definition lays - a call, a branch - goes
\ in a table (RT+), allocated for the definition and freed at its end, so
\ that a forward branch can be laid short when it is resolved: the code
\ it skips moved back the 3 or 4 bytes saved, and every recorded field
\ that move breaks re-aimed (REL-FIX, native-rt.4). 692's first try had
\ no table, so it shortened only branches that skipped nothing relative:
\ 605 of 2,933, and the shrinker cost what it saved.
VARIABLE RT-AT      \ the table: field, target, width - three cells an entry
VARIABLE RT-N       \ entries in it
VARIABLE RT-FULL    \ set: no room left, this definition's branches stay long
VARIABLE LAST-LEAVE \ where the last LEAVE's link was laid - pending, so a move must not pass it
VARIABLE SHORT-OFF  \ set: forward branches stay long (starts at 0: the cross compiler lays it)
: RT+ ( f t w --- )   \ a relative field laid at f, aimed at t, w bytes wide
  RT-AT @ 0= IF  12288 ALLOCATE IF  DROP -1 RT-FULL !  ELSE  RT-AT !  THEN  THEN
  RT-N @ 511 > RT-AT @ 0= OR IF  DROP 2DROP  -1 RT-FULL !  EXIT  THEN
  RT-AT @ RT-N @ RT-PUT  1 RT-N +! ;
: RT-DONE ( --- )   RT-AT @ ?DUP IF FREE DROP THEN  0 RT-AT !  0 RT-N !  0 RT-FULL !  0 LAST-LEAVE ! ;
: REL, ( addr --- )   HERE OVER 4 RT+  HERE 4 + - ,4 ;       \ rel32 to addr, from the end of the field
: RDROP16, ( --- )   72 C, 131 C, 196 C, 16 C, ;                         \ add rsp,16

\ ---- the back end proper ---------------------------------------------------------
: NO-PEEP ;                                   \ no peephole optimiser natively, yet
VARIABLE DDP         \ (672) the other pointer: data's while code is laid, code's while data is
VARIABLE IN-DATA     \ HERE is data's: from CREATE to the next definition
: EXIT, ( --- )   195 C, ;                    \ ret
\ Inlining (646): a colon definition whose body is copyable - no call, no
\ jump, no ret before its end, nothing of the return stack - is laid by `;`
\ with the primitives' marker, EB 01 len, so COMPILE, copies it inline.
\ Copyable because position-independent: a jump inside a definition is
\ relative and stays inside it - both ends move together, when `;`
\ shifts the body three bytes for the marker and when COMPILE, copies it
\ (651; 646 refused any jump). A call is relative to code outside, a ret
\ before the end would return from the caller, the return stack's words
\ may reach the caller's return address: those still make it uncopyable.
VARIABLE INL-OK      \ the definition being compiled can still be copied
VARIABLE BODY-AT     \ where its body begins
: CALL, ( xt --- )   0 INL-OK !  232 C, REL, ;     \ call rel32
VARIABLE LIT-AT       \ where the last short literal's push began (628)
VARIABLE LIT-VAL      \ and its value
VARIABLE LIT-END      \ and where it ended: 13 bytes on, or 15 (687)
VARIABLE FOLD-BARRIER \ the last place a jump lands: nothing before it is rewound
: LIT, ( x --- )   \ push it, in the shortest load that holds it (687)
  \ mov ebx,imm32 (5 bytes, zero-extended) for 0 to 2^32-1; mov rbx,imm32
  \ (7, sign-extended) for a negative that fits; movabs (10) else. The
  \ folds take a short literal's value as a sign-extended imm32, so those
  \ from 2^31 on are laid unfoldable. The 7-byte form was all of them
  \ until 687: 5,691 loads, 16.6 KB of the shell (NATIVE.md 14).
  \ (692) 0 by xor ebx,ebx (2 bytes): it sets the flags, which no fold
  \ reads across a literal - FRESH-CMP? and its kin want the compare to be
  \ the last thing laid - and the processor takes it as a zeroing, with no
  \ wait on rbx. Judged at 690 inside the A/B's floor, which the user
  \ rules "not slower" (692). -1 by or rbx,-1 was left out: or reads rbx,
  \ so a TRUE would wait on the cell under it (fn 1.028).
  DUP 0= IF  DROP  HERE LIT-AT !  0 LIT-VAL !  PUSH,  49 C, 219 C,  HERE LIT-END !  EXIT  THEN
  DUP 0< 0= OVER 2147483648 < AND IF  HERE LIT-AT !  DUP LIT-VAL !  PUSH,  187 C, ,4  HERE LIT-END !  EXIT  THEN
  DUP 0< 0= OVER 4294967296 < AND IF  PUSH,  187 C, ,4  0 LIT-AT !  EXIT  THEN
  DUP -2147483648 < 0= OVER 0< AND IF  HERE LIT-AT !  DUP LIT-VAL !  PUSH,  72 C, 199 C, 195 C, ,4  HERE LIT-END !  EXIT  THEN
  PUSH,  72 C, 187 C, ,  0 LIT-AT ! ;
: MARK-TARGET ( --- )   HERE FOLD-BARRIER ! ;   \ a jump lands here
: FRESH-LIT? ( --- f )   \ the last thing laid is a short literal, no jump into it
  LIT-AT @ ?DUP IF  LIT-END @ HERE =  SWAP FOLD-BARRIER @ < 0= AND  ELSE 0 THEN ;
: OP-IMM, ( modrm --- )   \ the literal unlaid; op rbx,imm32 in its place
  LIT-AT @ HERE - ALLOT  0 LIT-AT !  72 C, 129 C, C,  LIT-VAL @ ,4 ;
VARIABLE LAST-XT    \ the primitive COMPILE, last copied (669), or -2 for I
VARIABLE LAST-AT    \ where its code began
VARIABLE LAST-END   \ and ended: fresh while that is still HERE
: FRESH-LAST? ( xt --- f )   \ was xt the last thing laid, no jump landing since?
  LAST-XT @ =  LAST-END @ HERE = AND  LAST-AT @ FOLD-BARRIER @ < 0= AND ;
: UNLAST, ( --- )   LAST-AT @ HERE - ALLOT  0 LAST-XT ! ;
VARIABLE DUP-LAID   \ where COMPILE, last laid an inline DUP (629)
VARIABLE OVER-LAID  \ and an inline OVER
VARIABLE CMP-AT     \ a folded compare's cmp: where it began, 0 none
VARIABLE CMP-CC     \ its setcc's condition
VARIABLE CMP-END    \ where its flag's sequence ended
VARIABLE DUP-AT     \ a DUP laid right before its literal: where, else 0
: CMP-IMM, ( setcc --- )   \ cmp rbx,imm32; setcc al; movzx rbx,al; neg rbx
  DUP CMP-CC !
  DUP-LAID @ 8 + LIT-AT @ =  DUP-LAID @ FOLD-BARRIER @ < 0= AND
  IF DUP-LAID @ ELSE 0 THEN DUP-AT !
  LIT-AT @ CMP-AT !
  251 OP-IMM,  15 C, C, 192 C,  72 C, 15 C, 182 C, 216 C,  72 C, 247 C, 219 C,
  HERE CMP-END ! ;
: LOAD-ABS, ( --- )   \ the literal an address: unlaid; push, then load from it
  LIT-AT @ HERE - ALLOT  0 LIT-AT !  PUSH, ;
: OVER-OP, ( opcode --- )   \ the OVER unlaid; op rbx,[rbp] in its place (629)
  OVER-LAID @ HERE - ALLOT  0 OVER-LAID !  72 C, C, 93 C, 0 C, ;
: OVER-OP? ( xt --- xt 0 | -1 )   \ OVER then + - AND OR XOR: one instruction
  OVER-LAID @ 12 + HERE =  OVER-LAID @ FOLD-BARRIER @ < 0= AND  0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] + = IF DROP 3 OVER-OP, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] - = IF DROP 43 OVER-OP, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] AND = IF DROP 35 OVER-OP, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] OR = IF DROP 11 OVER-OP, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] XOR = IF DROP 51 OVER-OP, -1 EXIT THEN
  0 ;
VARIABLE LOAD-AT      \ a VARIABLE's fetch just laid - push, mov rbx,[a] - where it began (662)
VARIABLE LOAD-END     \ where it ended
VARIABLE LOAD-ADDR    \ the address it loads
: UNLIT, ( --- )   LIT-AT @ HERE - ALLOT  0 LIT-AT ! ;          \ the literal unlaid (645)
: POP, ( --- )   72 C, 139 C, 93 C, 0 C,  72 C, 131 C, 197 C, 8 C, ;   \ mov rbx,[rbp]  add rbp,8
: FOLD ( xt --- xt 0 | -1 )   \ (628) a literal then +, -, AND, OR, XOR, =, <, >,
  \ @ or C@: one instruction with the literal as its operand
  FRESH-LIT? 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] + = IF DROP 195 OP-IMM, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] - = IF DROP 235 OP-IMM, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] AND = IF DROP 227 OP-IMM, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] OR = IF DROP 203 OP-IMM, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] XOR = IF DROP 243 OP-IMM, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] = = IF DROP 148 CMP-IMM, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] < = IF DROP 156 CMP-IMM, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] > = IF DROP 159 CMP-IMM, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] @ = IF DROP LIT-AT @ >R  LOAD-ABS,  72 C, 139 C, 28 C, 37 C,  LIT-VAL @ ,4
    R> LOAD-AT !  LIT-VAL @ LOAD-ADDR !  HERE LOAD-END !  -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] C@ = IF DROP LOAD-ABS,  72 C, 15 C, 182 C, 28 C, 37 C,  LIT-VAL @ ,4 -1 EXIT THEN
  \ and a literal address then ! C! +! (645): the store to it, the value
  \ already the top once the literal is unlaid - a VARIABLE's update in one
  \ instruction and a pop, where it was a push, a load and a store
  DUP ['] ! = IF DROP UNLIT,  72 C, 137 C, 28 C, 37 C,  LIT-VAL @ ,4  POP, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] C! = IF DROP UNLIT,  136 C, 28 C, 37 C,  LIT-VAL @ ,4  POP, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] +! = IF DROP UNLIT,  72 C, 1 C, 28 C, 37 C,  LIT-VAL @ ,4  POP, -1 EXIT THEN
  0 ;
\ A compare of two cells, or of one with 0, followed by IF WHILE or UNTIL
\ (661): its flag was made - setcc, neg - popped and tested, 629 fused
\ only a compare with a literal. ?BRANCH, now unlays the copied compare
\ and lays the cmp or test, the pops by mov and lea, which keep the
\ flags, and the jump taken when it is false. The jcc is read from the
\ primitive's own setcc - not when its code is not the shape expected.
VARIABLE CMP2-AT     \ a compare just copied: where it began, 0 none
VARIABLE CMP2-END    \ where it ended
VARIABLE CMP2-JCC    \ 0F's second byte for the jump taken when it is false
VARIABLE CMP2-CELLS  \ how many cells it compares: 2, or 1 with 0
: SETCC-AT ( xt offset --- jcc true | false )   \ 0F 9x C3 there: jcc-not 8x^1
  SWAP 3 + +  DUP C@ 15 = OVER 2 + C@ 195 = AND IF 1+ C@ 1 XOR 16 - TRUE ELSE DROP 0 THEN ;
: CMP2? ( xt --- jcc cells true | false )
  DUP ['] 0< = IF DROP 137 1 TRUE EXIT THEN                      \ sar rbx,63: jns
  DUP ['] 0= = IF 8 SETCC-AT IF 1 TRUE ELSE 0 THEN EXIT THEN  \ test, sete: jne
  DUP ['] = = OVER ['] < = OR OVER ['] > = OR OVER ['] U< = OR OVER ['] <> = OR
  IF 16 SETCC-AT IF 2 TRUE ELSE 0 THEN EXIT THEN  DROP 0 ;
\ A VARIABLE's fetch folded into the operation after it (662): `X @ +` laid
\ push, mov rbx,[X], then the add's load and pop of the cell just pushed - a
\ round trip through memory, which priced at 11-15 % of every workload
\ (one more at every push, A/B). Now + - AND OR XOR take [X] as their
\ operand, = < > U< <> compare with it - the flag made as before, or the
\ branch after it fused (kind 0: the cmp laid, one cell to pop) - and >R
\ pushes it straight from memory. Never across a jump's target.
: FRESH-LOAD? ( --- f )   LOAD-AT @ DUP IF  LOAD-END @ HERE =  SWAP FOLD-BARRIER @ < 0= AND  THEN ;
: MEM-OP, ( op --- )   \ the fetch unlaid; op rbx,[X] in its place
  LOAD-AT @ HERE - ALLOT  0 LOAD-AT !  72 C, C, 28 C, 37 C,  LOAD-ADDR @ ,4 ;
: MFOLD ( xt --- xt 0 | -1 )
  FRESH-LOAD? 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] + = IF DROP 3 MEM-OP, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] - = IF DROP 43 MEM-OP, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] AND = IF DROP 35 MEM-OP, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] OR = IF DROP 11 MEM-OP, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] XOR = IF DROP 51 MEM-OP, -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP ['] >R = IF DROP  LOAD-AT @ HERE - ALLOT  0 LOAD-AT !         \ push qword [X]
    255 C, 52 C, 37 C,  LOAD-ADDR @ ,4  0 INL-OK !  -1 EXIT THEN
  DUP CMP2? IF  2 = IF  CMP2-JCC !  DROP  59 MEM-OP,                \ cmp rbx,[X]
      HERE CMP2-AT !  0 CMP2-CELLS !                                 \ mov ebx,0  setcc bl  neg rbx
      187 C, 0 ,4  15 C, CMP2-JCC @ 1 XOR 16 + C, 195 C,  72 C, 247 C, 219 C,
      HERE CMP2-END !  -1 EXIT  THEN  DROP  THEN
  0 ;
\ Pushes their next word takes straight back (669), from one build's
\ count of what follows each push (NATIVE.md 12): R> DROP is add rsp,8;
\ DUP >R is push rbx; R@ + is add rbx,[rsp]; I + is add rbx,r14 - no
\ cell to the data stack and back. In ?BRANCH,, ?DUP DUP and DUP 0= or
\ DUP 0< before IF WHILE UNTIL: test rbx,rbx and the jump.
: PAIR, ( xt --- xt 0 | -1 )
  DUP ['] DROP = IF  ['] R> FRESH-LAST? IF DROP UNLAST,  72 C, 131 C, 196 C, 8 C,  -1 EXIT THEN THEN
  DUP ['] >R = IF  ['] DUP FRESH-LAST? IF DROP UNLAST,  83 C,  0 INL-OK !  -1 EXIT THEN THEN
  DUP ['] + = IF  ['] R@ FRESH-LAST? IF DROP UNLAST,  72 C, 3 C, 28 C, 36 C,  -1 EXIT THEN
                  -2 FRESH-LAST? IF DROP UNLAST,  76 C, 1 C, 243 C,  -1 EXIT THEN THEN
  0 ;
: LIT-WORD? ( xt --- x true | xt false )   \ (627) code that only pushes a
  \ constant and returns - a CONSTANT, a VARIABLE, a CREATE no DOES> has
  \ patched, `: FIVE 5 ;` - push rbx, mov rbx imm32 or movabs imm64, ret
  DUP @ 26328115314525000 = 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP 8 + C@ 187 = OVER 13 + C@ 195 = AND IF  9 + @4  TRUE EXIT THEN    \ mov ebx,imm32 (687)
  DUP 8 + C@ 49 = OVER 9 + C@ 219 = AND OVER 10 + C@ 195 = AND IF  DROP 0 TRUE EXIT THEN   \ xor ebx,ebx (692)
  DUP 8 + C@ 72 = 0= IF 0 EXIT THEN
  DUP 9 + C@ 199 = OVER 10 + C@ 195 = AND OVER 15 + C@ 195 = AND IF
    11 + @4  DUP 2147483647 > IF 4294967296 - THEN  TRUE EXIT THEN   \ sign-extended
  DUP 9 + C@ 187 = OVER 18 + C@ 195 = AND IF  10 + @  TRUE EXIT THEN
  0 ;
: COMPILE, ( xt --- )   \ an inline primitive's code, copied; a pushing word's
  \ push, inline (627); a literal folded into the operation after it (628);
  \ anything else, called
  FOLD IF EXIT THEN
  MFOLD IF EXIT THEN
  PAIR, IF EXIT THEN
  OVER-OP? IF EXIT THEN
  DUP C@ 235 = OVER 1+ C@ 1 = AND IF
    DUP ['] DUP = IF HERE DUP-LAID ! THEN  DUP ['] OVER = IF HERE OVER-LAID ! THEN
    DUP ['] EXIT = OVER ['] >R = OR OVER ['] R> = OR OVER ['] R@ = OR
    OVER ['] RP@ = OR OVER ['] RP! = OR IF 0 INL-OK ! THEN      \ not copyable (646)
    DUP CMP2? IF CMP2-CELLS ! CMP2-JCC ! HERE CMP2-AT ! ELSE 0 CMP2-AT ! THEN
    DUP LAST-XT !  HERE LAST-AT !
    DUP 2 + C@ >R  3 + HERE R@ CMOVE  R> ALLOT  HERE CMP2-END !  HERE LAST-END !  EXIT  THEN
  LIT-WORD? IF LIT, EXIT THEN
  CALL, ;

\ forward and backward jumps: a 4-byte field, patched when its target comes
: >MARK ( --- a-addr )   HERE 0 ,4 ;
: SHORT-OK? ( a-addr --- f )   \ the branch whose rel32 field is at a-addr, laid short?
  DUP HERE SHORT-FITS?  SWAP 4 + LAST-LEAVE @ > AND  RT-FULL @ SHORT-OFF @ OR 0= AND ;
VARIABLE SH-MOVED   \ what the last >RESOLVE moved the code back by: 0, 3 or 4
: SHORTEN ( a-addr --- )   \ (695) SHORT-MOVE does the work, in assembly
  >R RT-AT @ RT-N @ R> HERE SHORT-MOVE  SH-MOVED !  SWAP HERE - ALLOT  HERE 1 RT+
  MARK-TARGET  0 LIT-AT !  0 CMP-AT !  0 CMP2-AT !  0 DUP-AT !
  0 LAST-XT !  0 LAST-END !  0 DUP-LAID !  0 OVER-LAID !  0 LOAD-AT !  0 LOAD-END ! ;
: >RESOLVE ( a-addr --- )
  0 SH-MOVED !  DUP SHORT-OK? IF SHORTEN EXIT THEN
  MARK-TARGET  DUP HERE 4 RT+  HERE OVER 4 + - SWAP !4 ;
: BACK, ( addr --- )   REL, ;

: JCC-NOT ( setcc --- jcc )   \ the jump taken when the comparison is false
  DUP 148 = IF DROP 133 EXIT THEN          \ sete -> jne
  DUP 156 = IF DROP 141 EXIT THEN          \ setl -> jge
  DROP 142 ;                               \ setg -> jle
: FRESH-CMP? ( --- f )   CMP-AT @ DUP IF  CMP-END @ HERE =  SWAP FOLD-BARRIER @ < 0= AND  THEN ;
: FRESH-CMP2? ( --- f )   CMP2-AT @ DUP IF  CMP2-END @ HERE =  SWAP FOLD-BARRIER @ < 0= AND  THEN ;
: CMP2-BRANCH, ( --- )   \ (661) the compare unlaid: cmp or test, the pops, jcc
  CMP2-CELLS @ 1 =  DUP-LAID @ 8 + CMP2-AT @ = AND  DUP-LAID @ FOLD-BARRIER @ < 0= AND IF
    DUP-LAID @ HERE - ALLOT  0 DUP-LAID !                 \ (669) DUP 0= IF: test, the jump
    72 C, 133 C, 219 C,  15 C, CMP2-JCC @ C,  0 CMP2-AT !  EXIT THEN
  CMP2-AT @ HERE - ALLOT
  CMP2-CELLS @ 2 = IF
    72 C, 139 C, 69 C, 0 C,  72 C, 57 C, 216 C,              \ mov rax,[rbp]  cmp rax,rbx
    72 C, 139 C, 93 C, 8 C,  72 C, 141 C, 109 C, 16 C,       \ mov rbx,[rbp+8]  lea rbp,[rbp+16]
  ELSE
    CMP2-CELLS @ IF  72 C, 133 C, 219 C,  THEN               \ test rbx,rbx; kind 0 (662): cmp laid
    72 C, 139 C, 93 C, 0 C,  72 C, 141 C, 109 C, 8 C,        \ mov rbx,[rbp]  lea rbp,[rbp+8]
  THEN  15 C, CMP2-JCC @ C,  0 CMP2-AT ! ;
: ?BRANCH, ( --- )   \ the flag popped and tested, the jump taken if false; after a
  \ compare just laid, the compare's own flags (629): DUP lit < IF is cmp, jge
  FRESH-CMP? IF
    DUP-AT @ ?DUP IF  HERE - ALLOT  72 C, 129 C, 251 C, LIT-VAL @ ,4       \ no copy made
    ELSE  CMP-AT @ 7 + HERE - ALLOT                                         \ keep the cmp;
      72 C, 139 C, 93 C, 0 C,  72 C, 141 C, 109 C, 8 C,  THEN               \ pop by mov, lea
    15 C, CMP-CC @ JCC-NOT C,
  ELSE  FRESH-CMP2? IF CMP2-BRANCH, ELSE
    ['] ?DUP FRESH-LAST? IF  UNLAST,                    \ (669) test, jnz past the drop
      72 C, 133 C, 219 C,  117 C, HERE DUP 14 + 1 RT+ 13 C,  72 C, 139 C, 93 C, 0 C,  72 C, 141 C, 109 C, 8 C,  233 C,   \ (693) the jnz recorded
    ELSE ['] DUP FRESH-LAST? IF  UNLAST,  72 C, 133 C, 219 C,  15 C, 132 C,    \ test, jz
    ELSE POPF,  15 C, 132 C,  THEN THEN  THEN  THEN
  0 CMP-AT ! ;
: IF      ?COMP  ?BRANCH, >MARK ; IMMEDIATE
: THEN    ?COMP  >RESOLVE ; IMMEDIATE
: ELSE    ?COMP  233 C, >MARK  SWAP >RESOLVE  SH-MOVED @ - ; IMMEDIATE      \ jmp
\ (693) the IF is resolved after ELSE's jmp is laid, so a shortened IF
\ moves that jmp's pending field back with the code: its address follows
: BEGIN   ?COMP  MARK-TARGET HERE ; IMMEDIATE
: UNTIL   ?COMP  ?BRANCH, BACK, ; IMMEDIATE
: AGAIN   ?COMP  233 C, BACK, ; IMMEDIATE
: WHILE   ?COMP  POSTPONE IF  SWAP ; IMMEDIATE
: REPEAT  ?COMP  POSTPONE AGAIN  POSTPONE THEN ; IMMEDIATE

\ counted loops, in registers (630): r14 the index, r13 the limit (r15
\ until 696, which frees r15 for the data stack: a base needing no
\ displacement byte - NATIVE.md 14); DO
\ saves the enclosing loop's pair on the return stack and the loop's end
\ puts it back - so a loop is `inc r14; cmp r14,r13; jne`, nothing in
\ memory, and a word called in a loop keeps the caller's loop as it was.
\ J is the pair saved last: [rsp]. A LEAVE is a jump to the loop's end,
\ where the pair is restored; 'LEAVE holds the newest one's field, and
\ each field, until patched, the distance back to the one before it.
: LEAVE-LINK, ( --- )
  'LEAVE @ ?DUP IF HERE SWAP - ELSE 0 THEN  HERE 'LEAVE !  ,4  HERE LAST-LEAVE ! ;   \ (693)
: RESOLVE-LEAVE ( outer --- )   \ every LEAVE of this loop: here; 'LEAVE as it was
  'LEAVE @ BEGIN ?DUP WHILE
    DUP @4 >R  DUP >RESOLVE  R> ?DUP IF - ELSE DROP 0 THEN
  REPEAT  'LEAVE ! ;
: LOOP-ENTER, ( --- )   \ push r13  push r14  mov r13,[rbp]  mov r14,rbx  mov rbx,[rbp+8]  add rbp,16
  65 C, 85 C,  65 C, 86 C,  76 C, 139 C, 109 C, 0 C,  73 C, 137 C, 222 C,
  72 C, 139 C, 93 C, 8 C,  72 C, 131 C, 197 C, 16 C, ;
: LOOP-EXIT, ( outer --- )   \ the LEAVEs here; pop r14  pop r13
  RESOLVE-LEAVE  65 C, 94 C, 65 C, 93 C, ;
: DO   ?COMP  LOOP-ENTER,  'LEAVE @  0 'LEAVE !  MARK-TARGET HERE ; IMMEDIATE
: ?DO  ?COMP  LOOP-ENTER,  'LEAVE @  0 'LEAVE !
  77 C, 57 C, 238 C,  15 C, 132 C, LEAVE-LINK,          \ cmp r14,r13  je the end: a LEAVE
  MARK-TARGET HERE ; IMMEDIATE
: LOOP  ?COMP   \ inc r14  cmp r14,r13  jne back
  73 C, 255 C, 198 C,  77 C, 57 C, 238 C,  15 C, 133 C, BACK,  LOOP-EXIT, ; IMMEDIATE
: +LOOP  ?COMP   \ native.4's crossing test, by signs, on r14 and r13
  72 C, 137 C, 216 C,  72 C, 139 C, 93 C, 0 C,  72 C, 131 C, 197 C, 8 C,   \ n into rax, popped
  76 C, 137 C, 242 C,  76 C, 41 C, 234 C,  73 C, 1 C, 198 C,             \ rdx=i-lim  i+=n
  73 C, 137 C, 208 C,  73 C, 1 C, 192 C,  73 C, 49 C, 208 C,  72 C, 49 C, 194 C,
  73 C, 33 C, 208 C,  15 C, 137 C, BACK,  LOOP-EXIT, ; IMMEDIATE
: LEAVE   ?COMP  233 C, LEAVE-LINK, ; IMMEDIATE
: I       ?COMP  HERE LAST-AT !  PUSH,  76 C, 137 C, 243 C,         \ mov rbx,r14
  HERE LAST-END !  -2 LAST-XT ! ; IMMEDIATE
: J       ?COMP  PUSH,  72 C, 139 C, 28 C, 36 C, ; IMMEDIATE   \ mov rbx,[rsp]
: UNLOOP  ?COMP  65 C, 94 C, 65 C, 93 C, ; IMMEDIATE           \ pop r14  pop r13

\ shadow.4's locals (637): shadow.4 lays them with OP, and SLOT, - CV8's
\ locals opcodes on a variable - so natively OP, records the operation and
\ SLOT, lays its code: LSAVE and LRESTORE inline, L! and LZERO inline. Only
\ these four: nothing else lays CV8 opcodes with them.
\ (655) LSAVE and LRESTORE come in runs - a definition's saves at its
\ entry, its restores at each exit - and a run is laid as one group: the
\ save stack's count read once into rcx, one bounds check for the run, two
\ instructions a slot through rax, the count updated once. They were a
\ call each, the count loaded, checked and stored again for every slot.
\ A group grows as SLOT, lays the next of its run: the count's update,
\ laid last, is unlaid, the slot laid, the update laid again, the check's
\ immediate patched - never across a jump's target, which would move.
\ Its checks jump to (L-OVER) and (L-UNDER), outside the body: a body
\ with locals is not copyable, as with the calls.
VARIABLE PENDING-OP
VARIABLE GRP-AT     \ where the group being laid began
VARIABLE GRP-OP     \ its op: 102, saves, or 103, restores
VARIABLE GRP-N      \ its slots so far
VARIABLE GRP-END    \ HERE when it was laid: the next slot extends it only there
: OP, ( op --- )   PENDING-OP ! ;
: GRP-START, ( op --- )   \ mov rcx,[count]  cmp rcx,imm32  ja (L-OVER) | jb (L-UNDER)
  HERE GRP-AT !  DUP GRP-OP !  0 GRP-N !
  72 C, 139 C, 12 C, 37 C,  LSAVE-SP ,4   72 C, 129 C, 249 C, 0 ,4
  15 C,  102 = IF 135 C, ['] (L-OVER) ELSE 130 C, ['] (L-UNDER) THEN  REL, ;
: GRP-SLOT, ( a-addr --- )   \ a save: mov rax,[a]  mov [rcx*8+stack+8n],rax;
  \ a restore, the newest first: mov rax,[rcx*8+stack-8(n+1)]  mov [a],rax
  GRP-OP @ 102 = IF
    72 C, 139 C, 4 C, 37 C, ,4   72 C, 137 C, 4 C, 205 C,  LSAVE-STK GRP-N @ CELLS + ,4
  ELSE
    72 C, 139 C, 4 C, 205 C,  LSAVE-STK GRP-N @ 1+ CELLS - ,4   72 C, 137 C, 4 C, 37 C, ,4
  THEN  1 GRP-N +! ;
: GRP-END, ( --- )   \ add | sub qword [count],n - and the check's immediate:
  \ a save overflows past LSAVE_MAX - n, a restore underflows below n
  72 C, 131 C,  GRP-OP @ 102 = IF 4 ELSE 44 THEN C,  37 C,  LSAVE-SP ,4  GRP-N @ C,
  GRP-OP @ 102 = IF LSAVE-LIM GRP-N @ - ELSE GRP-N @ THEN  GRP-AT @ 11 + !4
  HERE GRP-END !  0 INL-OK ! ;
: LGROUP, ( a-addr op --- )
  DUP GRP-OP @ =  GRP-END @ HERE = AND  FOLD-BARRIER @ GRP-AT @ > 0= AND
  IF  DROP  -9 ALLOT  ELSE  GRP-START,  THEN  GRP-SLOT,  GRP-END, ;
: SLOT, ( a-addr --- )
  PENDING-OP @  0 PENDING-OP !
  DUP 102 = OVER 103 = OR IF LGROUP, EXIT THEN
  DUP 104 = IF DROP 72 C, 137 C, 28 C, 37 C, ,4                   \ mov [a],rbx
    72 C, 139 C, 93 C, 0 C,  72 C, 131 C, 197 C, 8 C, EXIT THEN    \ the top popped
  DUP 105 = IF DROP 72 C, 199 C, 4 C, 37 C, ,4  0 ,4 EXIT THEN     \ mov qword [a],0
  TRUE ABORT" native: OP, and SLOT, lay only shadow.4's locals" ;

\ CATCH, keeping a register loop's pair across it: kernel.4's, bracketed
: CATCH0 ( i*x xt --- j*x 0 | i*x n )   CATCH ;
: CATCH ( i*x xt --- j*x 0 | i*x n )   (SAVE-LOOP) CATCH0 (RESTORE-LOOP) ;

\ ---- definitions ----------------------------------------------------------------
\ (672) CREATE's data in a region of its own (NATIVE.md 13): DP and DDP
\ trade places, so HERE ALLOT , and C, lay data after a CREATE and code
\ once a definition begins - and DICT-LIMIT, through the runtime's cell,
\ is data's limit or code's. 626 had the data on the code's next line:
\ every page of the code with a variable on it written, and padding.
: DATA-SWAP ( --- )   DP @  DDP @ DP !  DDP ! ;
: DATA-ON ( --- )   IN-DATA @ 0= IF  DATA-SWAP  -1 IN-DATA !  DATA-TOP DLIMIT-CELL !  THEN ;
: DATA-OFF ( --- )   IN-DATA @ IF  DATA-SWAP  0 IN-DATA !  0 DLIMIT-CELL !  THEN ;
: DATA-ALIGN ( --- )   DATA-OFF ;
: DATA-BASE ( --- addr )   DATA-START ;     \ where data's region begins, for SAVE-SYSTEM
: :  ( "name" --- )   DATA-ALIGN !CSP HEADER ]  HERE BODY-AT !  -1 INL-OK !  RT-DONE ;
: INLINE-MARK ( --- )   \ a copyable body of 1 to 64 bytes: moved up three, marked
  HERE BODY-AT @ - DUP 0 > OVER 65 < AND INL-OK @ AND IF
    >R  BODY-AT @ DUP 3 + R@ MOVE  3 ALLOT
    235 BODY-AT @ C!  1 BODY-AT @ 1+ C!  R> BODY-AT @ 2 + C!
  ELSE DROP THEN ;
: ;  ( --- )   ?COMP  INLINE-MARK  EXIT, [ ?CSP REVEAL  RT-DONE ; IMMEDIATE
: RECURSE ( --- )   ?COMP  LAST @ NAME> CALL, ; IMMEDIATE
: CREATE ( "name" --- )   \ the 24-byte stub; the data in data's region (672)
  DATA-OFF  HEADER REVEAL  DDP @ 7 + -8 AND DUP DDP !
  PUSH,  72 C, 199 C, 195 C,  ,4  195 C,  8 0 DO 144 C, LOOP  DATA-ON ;
: >BODY ( xt --- a-addr )   11 + @4 ;          \ the address in the stub's mov
: CONSTANT ( x "name" --- )   DATA-ALIGN HEADER REVEAL  LIT, EXIT, ;
: (;CODE) ( --- )   \ the last created word jumps to what follows the call to this,
  \ the data's address pushed already; R> ends the defining word
  R> LAST @ NAME> 15 +  233 OVER C!  1+ SWAP OVER 4 + - SWAP !4 ;
\ S" in a definition (666): the string's bytes jumped over, and its address
\ by a rip-relative lea, then its length - where (S") was a call whose ret
\ went to the byte after the string, so the return predictor missed every
\ one. Position-independent: a body with a string literal can be moved and
\ inlined. 2 or 5 bytes of jmp, the bytes, 27 of pushes; (S") was 6 and
\ the bytes. ." and ABORT" keep their runtimes: they print, or abort.
: SLIT, ( c-addr u --- )
  DUP 128 < OVER 1 <> AND IF 235 C, DUP C, ELSE 233 C, DUP ,4 THEN   \ jmp over the bytes
  \ - never jmp +1, EB 01: at a body's start that reads as the inline
  \ marker, and COMPILE, copied a body beginning `S" !"` for code (666)
  HERE >R  2DUP HERE SWAP MOVE  DUP ALLOT  SWAP DROP  MARK-TARGET   \ the bytes; the jmp lands here
  72 C, 131 C, 237 C, 16 C,  72 C, 137 C, 93 C, 8 C,      \ sub rbp,16  mov [rbp+8],rbx
  72 C, 141 C, 5 C,  R> HERE 4 + - ,4                     \ lea rax,[rip - back to the bytes]
  72 C, 137 C, 69 C, 0 C,                                 \ mov [rbp],rax
  187 C, ,4 ;                                             \ mov ebx,u
: S"  ( "ccc<quote>" --- )
  STATE @ IF 34 PARSE SLIT,
          ELSE 34 PARSE POCKET PLACE POCKET COUNT THEN ; IMMEDIATE
: DOES> ( --- )   ?COMP  POSTPONE (;CODE) ; IMMEDIATE
: POSTPONE ( "name" --- )
  ?COMP  BL WORD FIND  ?DUP 0= ABORT" not found"
  0< IF  LIT,  ['] COMPILE, CALL,  ELSE  COMPILE,  THEN ; IMMEDIATE
END-CROSS
